acher.html with Load/Rename/Add more Quiz controls, Dashboard navigation button, auto-named student HTML downloads (e.g. Quiz 1.html / custom name), multi-quiz vault routing in index.html, and verification across all affected flows.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","Content":"\"# Implementation Plan — Teacher Quiz Dashboard, Multi-Quiz Switching & Auto-Named Student Downloads (`Patch 1.0.25`)\\n\\n## Investigation Summary & Findings\\n1. **Current Single-Quiz Coupling (`teacher.html` & `index.html`):**\\n   - `teacher.html` initializes a fixed `const quizId = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get(\\\"quiz\\\") || \\\"active\\\"` once at startup, always lands directly in `#view-editor`, and hardcodes `'index.html'` inside `triggerDownload()` and `finalizeDownload()`.\\n   - `index.html` hardcodes fallback `\\\"active\\\"` when `?quiz=` is missing from the URL. Consequently, a downloaded standalone quiz file for Quiz 2 (`quiz_2.html`) opened offline/from disk would read/submit to `\\\"active\\\"` (Quiz 1) and collide on `localStorage` lock key `ds_quiz_lock_active` unless `quizId` is sealed into `#local-db-vault` and read before initializing `LOCK`.\\n2. **Live Firestore Collection State (`sir-jasper-quiz`):**\\n   - Currently `quizzes` holds `active` (`title: \\\"C Programming: Switch Case Quizasdasdsss\\\"`) and `template` (~`364KB` compiled HTML).\\n   - Verified via read-only test that Firestore REST `POST :runQuery` with `select` projection (`['label', 'quizOrder', 'title']`) returns `HTTP 200` in ~`523 bytes` without requiring custom indexes and completely avoids transferring `template`'s `364KB` `html` field or full `questions` arrays during Dashboard loads.\\n\\n## Research & Optimization Rationale\\n- **Masked Projection Listing (`:runQuery` with `select`):** Fetching only metadata (`label`, `quizOrder`, `title`) cuts Dashboard payload size from hundreds of kilobytes to `< 1KB` as quiz count grows.\\n- **DRY Partial Patch Helper:** Generalizing `patchField(id, fieldName, val)` into `patchFields(id, fieldsObj)` (building multiple `updateMask.fieldPaths=...` params) handles both single-field `lockEpoch` updates and atomic two-field `{ label, quizOrder }` renames without duplicating HTTP/error logic.\\n- **Single-Pass `#local-db-vault` Decode (`index.html`):** Decoding `#local-db-vault` once at startup\n<truncated 8096 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\CxAdmin\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\\\implementation_plan.md\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking","tool_calls"]}
